{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1766,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A driver took one wrong turn, and stopped right in front of an assassin.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 104
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Sarajevo, June twenty-eighth, nineteen fourteen. Archduke Franz Ferdinand, heir to the throne, rides in an open car.",
   "from": 107,
   "to": 303
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That morning, a young man throws a bomb.",
   "from": 307,
   "to": 372
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "crowd",
   "text": "Bomb!",
   "from": 376,
   "to": 393
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It bounces off and blows up under the next car.",
   "from": 396,
   "to": 461
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The plot seems dead. Another plotter, nineteen-year-old Gavrilo Princip, drifts to a street corner.",
   "from": 465,
   "to": 596
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The Archduke changes plans. He'll visit the wounded in hospital.",
   "from": 599,
   "to": 665
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But nobody tells the drivers.",
   "from": 669,
   "to": 754
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The car in front turns down the old route. His driver follows.",
   "from": 758,
   "to": 838
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "governor",
   "text": "Wrong way! Stop!",
   "from": 841,
   "to": 873
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The driver brakes to reverse. It stops, a few steps from Princip.",
   "from": 876,
   "to": 955
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Two shots. The Archduke and his wife Sophie are killed.",
   "from": 959,
   "to": 1032
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, Austria blamed Serbia, and declared war one month later. Russia backed Serbia. Germany backed Austria. France backed Russia.",
   "from": 1048,
   "to": 1238
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Within a week, most of Europe was at war. About twenty million would die. Four empires would fall.",
   "from": 1241,
   "to": 1395
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Now, what if the driver had known? The car speeds past, and Princip probably never gets his shot.",
   "from": 1399,
   "to": 1549
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Would war have come anyway? Many historians think so. But not that day, and not from that spark.",
   "from": 1553,
   "to": 1677
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And that spark came down to one wrong turn.",
   "from": 1680,
   "to": 1742
  }
 ],
